        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Artist Alexander Calder's mobiles come to life in a Paris exhibition Issued on: 15/04/2026 - 11:59 Three pieces of wire and string, a clothespin, a cork – these humble materials gave rise to the famous sculptures of American artist Alexander Calder, now on majestic display at the Louis Vuitton Foundation in Paris. Some 300 works, including 139 sculptures and 33 paintings, will enliven the vast galleries until August 16, as well as, for the first time, the museum’s garden designed by the American-Canadian architect Frank Gehry, who passed away in December 2025. Pope to urge peace in Cameroon's conflict zone 15/04/2026 Peru candidate demands vote annulment as count tightens 15/04/2026 War and Peace: Israel brings Lebanon to negotiating table as airstrikes rain down on Beirut 15/04/2026 Middle East Paris Saint-Germain beats Liverpool to reach the Champions League semifinals 15/04/2026 Frenchman scoops up 1 million euro Picasso painting in Paris raffle 15/04/2026 Lebanese 'cautiously optimistic' as talks with Israel unfold in Washington 15/04/2026 France and UK to co-host Hormuz shipping security talks 15/04/2026 New trial over Maradona's death begins in Argentina 15/04/2026 Israeli army issues new evacuation call to south Lebanon residents 15/04/2026"
